# Documents vs folders (terminology)

When the user shares a **ref**, mockup, or talks about the left panel / canvas / timeline, use this mapping — do **not** confuse labels with the old model.

## Mapping

| User / UI language | Means | Old name (avoid assuming) |
|---|---|---|
| **Document** / documento | Scheduled content unit on canvas & timeline (chip, schedule, body) | **Macronodo** / node card |
| **Documents** (sidebar section) | **Folders** — category boxes that contain documents | Panel that used to imply “docs list” only |
| **Folder** / caja / box | Folder container in Documents sidebar | — |

## Rules

- **Macronodos = documentos.** A “macronode” ref is a **document**, not a folder.
- **“Documents” (panel) = folders.** Opening Documents shows **folder boxes**; inside each box are the **documents**.
- Timeline / product model still holds: folder = class/category; document = scheduled unit (`anchorDate` / `anchorTime` / etc.).
- In copy and code comments prefer **document** / **folder** over macronode unless fixing legacy identifiers.

## Quick check

- Ref of a **box with children** → folder.
- Ref of a **single scheduled unit / canvas chip / open editor** → document (ex-macronode).
